{
  "name": "595. A custom provider's allowed_requests is enforced on every base before any upstream call (custom provider allowed requests)",
  "description": "TXE-7370, security. Local fixture regression, no live provider calls: start tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs, start an isolated gateway on tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json and run with providerErrorFixture=1; every case is skipped otherwise. A custom provider's allowed_requests is the operator's least-privilege control. Each provider method used to check it on its own, and the chat methods of the deepseek, glm, moonshot, qwen and xai bases did not, so a chat request reached the vendor with the custom provider's keys although chat was not allowed. Core now checks allowed_requests for every request type before it picks a key. The fixture config has one custom provider on each of those bases (gate_deepseek, gate_glm, gate_moonshot, gate_qwen, gate_xai) that allows only embedding, each with base_url on the fixture's /pp/ownkey, where every POST is kept in /__wire. Rows 1 to 5 send a chat request to each and assert a 400 unsupported_operation and that no call reached the fixture. Row 6 sends the same request streamed to gate_deepseek: chat_completion_stream is not allowed either. Row 7 is the control: gate_deepseek_chat allows chat_completion, and its request is answered with one call carrying its own key. core/allowedrequests_test.go covers every request type.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "[EXPECT-400] 595.1 gate_deepseek/fx-gate - chat is refused on a deepseek-based custom provider that does not allow it (custom provider allowed requests)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"gate_deepseek/fx-gate\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"hi\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "chat",
            "completions"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixtureUrl') + '/__reset', method: 'POST' }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('custom provider allowed requests setup: the fixture was reset', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null);",
              "    pm.expect(res.code).to.equal(200);",
              "  });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('400 unsupported_operation from the gateway', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text().slice(0, 400)).to.eql(400);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('unsupported_operation');",
              "});",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixtureUrl') + '/__wire', method: 'GET' }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('the fixture answered /__wire', function () { pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null); pm.expect(res.code).to.equal(200); });",
              "  var calls = res.json().data[0].calls;",
              "  pm.test('no call reached the upstream', function () { pm.expect(calls, JSON.stringify(calls).slice(0, 600)).to.have.length(0); });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
